arsi now I  have spoken to tutors in Polish in Greek  in Czech in Romanian and I can still  remember my polish teacher who lives in  Krakow and in Ukrainian our Ukrainian  teacher he lives in l'viv of course in  Arabic I had a teacher who was a Syrian  refugee located in Turkey I had a person  from Kuwait who was a student in Spain  and now I have this excellent tutor from  Egypt and I'm talking to him every day  what I do is when we talk and  particularly ibrahim in' in egypt he  makes copious notes of all of the words  and phrases that i struggled to find or  that I use incorrectly and then this is  sent to me as a report and and in fact  he's now started recording these and so  these are words and phrases that are  very alive to me because his these are  things that I tried to say and so when I  go back to him the next day you know I  still forget the same words I still make  the same mistakes but I'm slowly  improving thanks to this sort of  engagement with content that's very  meaningful to me this morning I went  through all of my conversation reports  which these these are imported as  lessons into link and I go back to  August and I can still remember this is  with this this student female student  from Kuwait who was living in Spain and  I can still remember our conversations  and so you can actually rehash your  conversations rehash the vocabulary you  discovered that some of the words that  were introduced then in which you  learned that you subsequently forgot you  are now coming across them again in  conversation and so I'm able to read and  more than once sort of go over again  these conversations so it's a  tremendously  useful way to not only get me speaking  but also helped me with my input based  learning and and not only that I'm able  to connect with Egypt with Syrian  refugee in Turkey with a Kuwaiti or yes  Kuwaiti living in Spain with with a  person in Warsaw Berlin Prague and very  often I follow up then with a visit as I  did in the case of 